; Target-neutral machine computation (docs/design.md, the behavioural
; model): fixed-width values and byte memory behind two signatures, with a
; concrete interpretation. An instruction's data effect is written once over
; these signatures and run in any interpretation. Depends on nothing; the
; layer audit keeps target vocabulary out.

(library
 (name compute)
 (public_name rivet.compute)
 (modes byte native)
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{env:RIVET_MELANGE=false} true)))
